    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "while this helps in some cases (different normalisation), this isn't actually what the client does:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/algolia/algoliasearch-client-javascript/blob/075b9fa2eeb83b12700d7c9c402f0520ab04681c/packages/transporter/src/createTransporter.ts#L88-L95\r\n\r\nit uses the params from the request to create the key, and therefore no normalisation is needed. Obviously it's annoying that we need to re-implement createMappedRequestOptions instead, but I think it's a more correct solution. Luckily its implementation isn't very big: \r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/algolia/algoliasearch-client-javascript/blob/3e4c225883b0099667e1a19713ba394bea0de7a3/packages/transporter/src/createMappedRequestOptions.ts#L3-L24",
    "commit_id": "3a3c579779e93dd75146fc5e4542cee3ed69c99a",
    "created_at": "2023-11-29T16:57:04Z",
    "diff_hunk": "@@ -56,9 +58,11 @@ export function hydrateSearchClient(\n           Object.keys(results).reduce(\n             (acc, key) =>\n               acc.concat(\n-                results[key].results.map((request) => ({\n-                  indexName: request.index,\n-                  params: request.params,\n+                results[key].results.map((result) => ({\n+                  indexName: result.index,\n+                  // We normalize the params received from the server as they can\n+                  // be serialized differently depending on the engine.\n+                  params: serializeQueryParameters(qs.parse(result.params)),",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/algolia/instantsearch/pull/5946#discussion_r1409603051",
